  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=-4-12(x-2)-5(x-2)^{2}-2(x-2)^{3}+(x-2)^{4}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${f}^{(4)}(2)?$",
  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of $(x-2)^{4}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{4!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{4!} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(4)}(2)}{24} & =1 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(2) & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
